<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτήσ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, and
		in <i><span class="en">
			Hp.
		</span></i>
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτος</span>):— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lasting a year</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένθος
				οὐκ ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				336
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστασία</span>
			f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.80
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτησίους ἄρχειν</span> to
			govern <i>for a year</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				60.24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>annual</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.993e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυσίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.11
				</span></i>
			, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1024.24
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Myconus</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.2227
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Thisbe</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτήσιοι πρόσιτ᾽ ἀεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					23
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βορέαι ἐ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτησίαι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				940a35
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πνεύματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Ind.</u>
					21.1
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίως</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				107
			</span></i>: neut. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυγόωσιν ἐτήσιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.226
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>).</div>
